/**
 * Every number box a person can type into, set to the edges of its band and to the values typed by
 * mistake, on real WinISD projects: the engine's output stays finite, nothing throws, nothing is slow
 * (T915; John, 18 Nov 2026: "ok look make the ap robust / and include proper limits on ui").
 *
 * The sweep itself is `../fixtures/inputLimitsSweep.ts`; the report of what breaks, with the cause
 * line and the proposed limit of each, is bugs/BUG_20261118_input-limits-sweep.md, regenerated by
 * `npx vite-node packages/design/test/domain/input-limits-sweep-report.ts`.
 *
 * Every case is the right expectation. The cases that break today are listed in `BREAKING_TODAY`
 * and run under `it.fails` naming that bug file; a fix turns its `it.fails` red, and the case then
 * moves out of the list to run as a plain test.
 */
